From ce19b583ec3b76f59c9ec3655755cd5b49d4fa08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <76759272+Cris7015@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:49:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] spi: airoha: sync SNFI MMIO access with Linux

Follow the controller-access conversion in airoha/kernel commit
038dd35b0 ("spi: airoha: remove regmap"). Replace the remaining CTRL
and NFI regmaps with mapped register bases and direct MMIO accesses.
Keep the separate SCU regmap used to query ARM bootstrap state.

Map the named ctrl/nfi resources, with an index fallback for existing
device trees. Preserve the SoC guards, EN751221 double-CS sequence,
DMA cleanup paths, direct W1C writes and existing polling timeouts.

Retain the ready-FIFO fast path from the preceding commit: U-Boot's
poll macro reads the timer before its first register access, so blindly
using it per byte would lose that part of the original optimization.

The identical driver source was tested on an Archer XR500v in a RAM
image based on its installed release, including the separate PHY-poll
fix. Three reads each of misc and fit matched CRC32 against installed
U-Boot. Median read times were 2.005/4.582 s for the installed release
and 2.026/4.643 s for the synchronized driver. The reference already
has the FIFO fast path; this is not a new speedup measurement.
TFTP worked on both sides and the RAM U-Boot booted installed Linux.
Neither the bootloader nor the persistent environment was flashed.

Full GCC builds passed for XR500v and EN7528. Clang 21 compiled the
SNFI object for MIPS, ARM32 and ARM64; full MIPS U-Boot still fails
on the existing k0 global-data register outside this driver. This
does not validate DMA hardware or full ARM builds.

Link: https://sirherobrine23.com.br/airoha/u-boot/pulls/11#issuecomment-6050
Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <76759272+Cris7015@users.noreply.github.com>
